    title: "twotimes函数图像性质 — Graphs of quadratic functions and their properties",
    mathExample: "y=x²−4x+3: a=1>0 opens up, minimum. Axis x=2. At x=2: y=−1. Turning point (2,−1). y=−x²+6x−5: a=−1<0 opens down, maximum. Axis x=3. At x=3: y=4. Turning point (3,4). Symmetric about x=−b/(2a).",
    boardWriting: "SMATH Week 68: Sec 2 N6.7 graphs of quadratic functions and their properties. Official three properties: (1) Sign of a (coefficient of x²): when a > 0 the graph opens upwards and has a minimum point; when a < 0 the graph opens downwards and has a maximum point. (2) Maximum and minimum points: the turning point. For y = ax² + bx + c, axis of symmetry is x = −b/(2a). The turning-point y-value is found by substituting that x. Friendly integers so −b/(2a) is an integer. (3) Symmetry: the graph is symmetric about the vertical line x = −b/(2a). Example 1: y = x² − 4x + 3. a = 1 > 0, opens upwards, has minimum. Axis x = −(−4)/(2×1) = 4/2 = 2. At x = 2: y = (2)² − 4(2) + 3 = 4 − 8 + 3 = −1. Turning point (2, −1). Symmetric about x = 2. Example 2: y = −x² + 6x − 5. a = −1 < 0, opens downwards, has maximum. Axis x = −6/(2×(−1)) = 3. At x = 3: y = −(3)² + 6(3) − 5 = 4. Turning point (3, 4). Symmetric about x = 3. This week is N6.7 ONLY: identify 「opens up/down」, name 「max vs min」, find axis x = k, find turning point (h, k) with friendly integers. Do NOT sketch from completed-square form or factorised form — that is 6.8. Fossil: sign error in −b/(2a); or forgetting to substitute after finding the axis; or saying 「opens upwards」 and 「has a maximum」 when a > 0 (wrong: a > 0 means minimum).",
