        teacherNotes: "Key questions 1: 'What is the relationship between congruent figures and similar figures?'Expected answer: 「Congruent figures are a special case of similar figures. Similar figures have the same shape but may have different sizes (corresponding sides in the same ratio k:1, where k can be any positive number). Congruent figures have the same shape AND the same size (k = 1, ratio 1:1). So congruent is similar with scale factor 1. All congruent figures are similar, but not all similar figures are congruent. Example: Two squares with side 5 cm are congruent (ratio 5:5 = 1:1) and similar (scale factor 1). Two squares with sides 5 cm and 10 cm are similar (ratio 5:10 = 1:2, scale factor 2) but not congruent.'(Ifchildcan't answer, guide: 'Congruent: 同形同大小, scale factor 1. Similar: 同形, 大小可not同, scale factor canis 1, 2, 3, 1:2, 2:3 wait. Congruent is similar 特例（scale factor = 1）. ')",
