        teacherNotes: "Key questions 2: 'Why does same area NOT mean similar?'Expected answer: 「Because similar figures must have the SAME SHAPE (corresponding angles equal and corresponding sides in the same ratio). Two figures can have the same area but different shapes. For example: Square A is 6 cm by 6 cm (area 36 cm²). Rectangle B is 9 cm by 4 cm (area 36 cm²). Same area (36 = 36), but different shapes (square vs rectangle). Square has all sides equal (6 = 6). Rectangle has sides not all equal (9 ≠ 4). Different shapes cannot be similar, even if same area. Similar is about SHAPE and RATIO, not area.'(Ifchildcan't answer, guide: 'Same area onlySayclear面积相wait, 但not能保证形状相同. 相似need求: 同形（corresponding angles equal）+ corresponds to边成比例（corresponding sides in the same ratio）. 面积相waitnot能保证this两点. so same area ≠ similar.')",
