        teacherNotes: "Learning objective: 'By the end of this lesson, you will be able to: (1) understand that scale factor k > 1 means enlargement (image is bigger than object); (2) understand that 0 < k < 1 means reduction (image is smaller than object); (3) understand the concept of centre of enlargement O (the fixed point from which distances are measured); (4) calculate image lengths using the formula: image length = k × object length; (5) understand that angles do NOT change (scale factor applies to lengths only, not angles). 成功标准 Success Criteria: You can identify whether k > 1 (enlargement) or 0 < k < 1 (reduction). You can calculate image lengths using k × object length. You understand that angles remain unchanged. You can draw simple diagrams showing object, image, and centre O.'",
