        teacherNotes: "Open screen share or whiteboard, writebelowthis weekHigh-frequency error: 'Fossil 1: k = 2 called a reduction (wrong classification)（k = 2 被称为缩小, 分类error）. Example: Triangle ABC enlarged by scale factor k = 2. Option says: 'k = 2 is a reduction because the number is less than 10.' ✗'Sayclear: 「This is a high-frequency error: k = 2 is放大not缩小. Wrong. k = 2 > 1, so it is an ENLARGEMENT (放大), not a reduction. Enlargement: k > 1 (image bigger). Reduction: 0 < k < 1 (image smaller). k = 2 means the image is 2 times the size of the object (double size, bigger). k = 1/2 (or 0.5) means the image is half the size of the object (smaller). Remember: k > 1 enlargement, 0 < k < 1 reduction. k = 2 > 1, so enlargement.'havechild repeatsone sentence: 'k > 1 is enlargement. k = 2 > 1, so enlargement.'againwriteWeektwoHigh-frequency error: 「Fossil 2: k = 1/2 called an enlargement (wrong classification)（k = 1/2 被称为放大, 分类error）. Example: Rectangle PQRS reduced by scale factor k = 1/2. Option says: 'k = 1/2 is an enlargement because we are multiplying.' ✗'Sayclear: 'This is a high-frequency error: k = 1/2 is缩小not放大. Wrong. k = 1/2 = 0.5 < 1, so it is a REDUCTION (缩小), not an enlargement. Yes, we multiply (image = k × object), but k = 1/2 < 1 means the image is SMALLER (half the size). k > 1: enlargement (bigger). 0 < k < 1: reduction (smaller). k = 1/2 < 1, so reduction.'havechild repeatsone sentence: 「0 < k < 1 is reduction. k = 1/2 < 1, so reduction.'againwriteWeekthreeHigh-frequency error: 'Fossil 3: Scale factor applied to an angle (angles do not scale)（缩放比例应useat角度, 角度not缩放）. Example: Triangle XYZ enlarged by k = 3. ∠X = 50°. Option says: 'Image ∠X' = 50° × 3 = 150°.' ✗」Sayclear: 「This is a high-frequency error: 角度not缩放. Wrong. Angles do NOT change. Scale factor k applies to side LENGTHS only, not to angles. If object has ∠X = 50°, then image has ∠X' = 50° (not 50° × 3 = 150°). Enlargement and reduction change the SIZE (side lengths), but the SHAPE (angles) stays the same. Same shape, different size = similar figures. Angles define shape. So angles do not scale. Remember: image length = k × object length (lengths scale). Image angle = object angle (angles do NOT scale).'havechild repeatsone sentence: 「Angles do not scale. Image angle = object angle.'againwriteWeek四化石error: 'Fossil 4: Two options that are the same object–image pair in a different order offered as two correct answers（两optionis同one物体-像对, 顺序not同, 作为两correctanswer）. Example: Triangle ABC → Triangle A'B'C' (k = 2). Options: (A) Object ABC, image A'B'C', k = 2. (B) Object A'B'C', image ABC, k = 1/2. Both marked correct ✗」Sayclear: 「This is a high-frequency error: 同one对图形顺序not同not能都选. Wrong. (A) and (B) describe the SAME pair of triangles, but in DIFFERENT directions. (A): ABC → A'B'C', k = 2 (enlargement). (B): A'B'C' → ABC, k = 1/2 (reduction, reverse direction). They are NOT the same transformation. In a question asking 'Which shows enlargement with k = 2?', only (A) is correct (ABC → A'B'C', k = 2). (B) is the reverse (reduction k = 1/2). Different object and image. Don't mark both. Read carefully: which is the OBJECT, which is the IMAGE. Object → image (one direction).'havechild repeatsone sentence: 'Object → image. Read the direction carefully.'",
