        teacherNotes: "Open screen share, playthis weekBoardWeike（3 example problem, each 2–3 min, total 8 min）. BoardWeike example 1: Triangle ABC enlarged by scale factor k = 3, centre O. AB = 2 cm. Find image side A'B'. Solution: Step 1: Check k. k = 3 > 1, so this is an enlargement (image bigger). Step 2: Use formula: image length = k × object length. Step 3: A'B' = k × AB = 3 × 2 = 6 cm. Check: 6 > 2, image is bigger. ✓ Answer: A'B' = 6 cm. BoardWeike example 2: Rectangle PQRS reduced by scale factor k = 1/2, centre O. PQ = 10 cm, QR = 8 cm. Find image sides P'Q' and Q'R'. Solution: Step 1: Check k. k = 1/2 = 0.5 < 1, so this is a reduction (image smaller). Step 2: Use formula: image length = k × object length. Step 3: P'Q' = k × PQ = 1/2 × 10 = 5 cm. Q'R' = k × QR = 1/2 × 8 = 4 cm. Check: 5 < 10, 4 < 8, image is smaller. ✓ Answer: P'Q' = 5 cm, Q'R' = 4 cm. BoardWeike example 3: Triangle XYZ enlarged by scale factor k = 4, centre O. ∠X = 45°. Find image angle ∠X'. Solution: Step 1: Angles do NOT change. Image angle = object angle. Step 2: ∠X' = ∠X = 45°. NOT 45° × 4 = 180°. Step 3: Scale factor k applies to side lengths only, not angles. Answer: ∠X' = 45°. Cast: secondary Wei, Aisha, Mr Lim at Riverside Secondary School. No calculator. Integer lengths only. this weekBoardWeikeuse: k = 3 triangle 2 cm, k = 1/2 rectangle 10-8 cm, k = 4 triangle 45°. Writing Q will use different numbers: k = 2 triangle 3 cm, k = 1/3 pentagon 6-9-12, k = 3 rectangle 40°. NOT the same.",
